    "changelog_excerpt": "# 🚀 DMTools Release v1.7.285\n\n## 📝 What's Changed\n\nFull diff: [v1.7.284...v1.7.285](https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/compare/v1.7.284...v1.7.285)\n\n### 🚀 Features\n- Create required labels automatically or on demand (#757) (#763) (c451c6f9)\n- Support conditional cliPrompts sections and single-prompt shorthand (IstiN/dmtools-agents#941) (#759) (a1969206)\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n- Skip quality workflow steps cleanly in empty repositories (#758) (#762) (c97ece7d)\n\n### 🛠 Maintenance\n- Update agents submodule to 26c58ded (#941, #1178) (#761) (d8ad1308)\n- Update coverage badge (#760) (44a6d696)\n- Update submodule for copilot model, guest dead-zone filter, and workflowRef (#765) (#766) (9c50ca84)\n\n---\n\nThis release includes the **DMTools CLI** and **Agent Skill** for enterprise dark-factory orchestration across MCP tools, AI agents, and delivery workflows.\n\n## 📦 What's Included\n\n### 🖥️ DMTools CLI\n- **Command-line interface** for DMTools operations\n- **Java-based** automation and integration tools\n- **Cross-platform install scripts** for easy setup (`install`, `install.sh`, `install.bat`, `install.ps1`)\n- **Wrapper script** (`dmtools.sh`)\n\n### 🤖 DMTools Agent Skill\n- **AI assistant skill** for MCP, AI agents, and generative-ai-friendly DMTools workflows in Cursor, Claude, Codex, and other Agent Skills compatible systems\n- **Complete DMtools documentation** (67+ MCP tools, JavaScript agent development, and configuration guides)\n- **Cross-platform support** (works with all major AI coding assistants)\n\n## 🎯 Quick Start\n\n### Install DMTools CLI\n\n**macOS / Linux / Git Bash:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\n```powershell\nirm https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/latest/download/install.ps1 | iex\n```\n\n### Install DMTools Agent Skill\n\n**macOS / Linux / Git Bash:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/download/v1.7.285/skill-install.sh | bash\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\n```po..."
